# Meta Repo AGENTS Guide

<!-- HELIX:BEGIN guide -->
Use this file to discover where relevant context lives in the installed Helix meta repo.

## Read Order

1. Read this file for repo-level source-of-truth rules
2. Read the nearest relevant subfolder `AGENTS.md`
3. Read only the targeted manifest, artifact, or prompt file
4. Prefer `index.md` plus targeted subdocuments over annexes or giant blobs

## Core Invariants

- `repos.yml` is the registry of known repos, not runtime state
- `.helix/repo-state/` contains generated readiness and scan results
- `.helix/context-providers.yml` controls whether optional retrieval layers such as code-review-graph are enabled
- `workspaces/<id>/workspace.yml` declares participating repos for a feature-space
- workspace artifacts live under `workspaces/<id>/`
- product code changes happen in attached repos, not in this meta repo

## Directory Map

| Path | Purpose | Start With |
|------|---------|------------|
| `.github/AGENTS.md` | Agent runtime surface | change agent behavior here |
| `.helix/AGENTS.md` | Runtime state and memory | active workspace, install state, repo-state |
| `workspaces/AGENTS.md` | Workspace artifact model | feature-space artifacts |
| `docs/AGENTS.md` | Human-facing docs | lifecycle and manifest docs |
| `templates/AGENTS.md` | Artifact and manifest templates | generated shapes |
| `scripts/AGENTS.md` | Installer, setup, and doctor scripts | operational tooling |

## Retrieval Rules

- Prefer workspace artifacts over explanatory docs when implementing
- Prefer `.helix/repo-state/<repo-id>.yml` over guessing repo readiness
- Prefer the workspace’s selected repos over broad registry scans
- Keep root `AGENTS.md` navigation-first
<!-- HELIX:END guide -->

## Local Overrides

Add org- or project-specific retrieval rules here. Helix sync preserves content outside managed sections.
